carriage previews, an enclosed C02 carriage with a working rigid door, a skinned horse, modular harness and coupled idle/walk/trot previews. Consolidates named resident authoring for existing reconstructed 1835 identities Otis Bardwell, Joseph Dufresne and Martin Flynn. Appearance, workwear and actions carry explicit reconstruction and license records.\n\nThe horse harness repair removes 100 original bind-pose crossings; the four changed parts have zero proper crossings and minimum 5.113 mm separation across 63 sampled idle/walk/trot poses. Other 32 harness parts and horse bytes are unchanged. Human expression inspection now reads all skinned meshes and restores exact defaults. Authored web exports use medium Meshopt with 16-bit normals, correcting the actual high-mode eight-bit normal failure without changing tolerances or generic fixture exports.\n\nThe new C02 study includes an actual-hierarchy door checker, five semantic negative controls and optional keyboard/touch door endpoints. The original source-history quotation is preserved; its working door is declared a development reconstruction. Optional paint/studio experiments remain outside this change.\n\nCurrent saved checkpoint: **512f4a7e372ec7dc89ebad20dfff6837b336cf97**, including dev fb6a775. Full preflight PASS: 1,015 checks, zero failed, 377 intentional self-tests; postcommit changelog/entry checks PASS. C02 local checks PASS: 15 door angles, five hierarchy negatives, eight desktop/mobile captures and measured isolation probes. These establish discrete surface/hierarchy behavior, not continuous sweep or solid containment.\n\nMerge qualification remains OPEN. At prior f97ee9497, the [canonical human workflow](https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/actions/runs/39220530645) passed 32 fixtures, 48 source/published resident inspections, six hierarchy/raw comparisons and 24 Khronos reports with zero errors/warnings. The published smoke matrix failed: 17/18 workflows passed, while [desktop stage 13](https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/actions/runs/39220627063) reported 331 draw calls against 330 and 31.23% HUD area against 10%. Actual failures and logs are preserved. A bounded targeted draw/HUD diagnostic is running against published 512f; no final replacement matrix has been dispatched yet. This PR remains draft until the failures are corrected and the final exact head is green.\n\nPhotographic quality, independent canonical image review, period construction acceptance, production LODs, loaded tack/reins, traffic, mounted riders and accessible boarding/riding remain open. Artifact downloads remain blocked by the unapplied environment policy. Outside horse/body/motion refinements are preserved separately. Merge target is dev only; production tickets remain open.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-18T20:37:49Z","updated_at":"2026-10-19T10:54:01Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"5c84888d522211f25cdce35d6d52b48f27d1079c","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"kevinrhaas:steward/period-transport-2793","ref":"steward/period-transport-2793","repo":{"id":1384299918,"node_id":"R_kgDOUoK9jg","name":"chicago","full_name":"kevinrhaas/chicago","owner":{"login":"kevinrhaas","id":4193586,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTM1ODY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4193586?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users